;; spec:   stdlib §2.1 rule 2 (an LSeq holds a Cell and does not cross a task), tranche 2 plan D7 (Proposed); types §1.3 (colour parameters)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  cannot be shared between threads
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: iterate take reduce
;; Proposed (plan recommendation, owner not yet confirmed; stdlib §8.2.1 item 14): the plan's Iterate is the
;; struct (Iterate a) with a field f of the type (fn (a) a). A function in a struct field has the colour :local
;; unless the struct has a colour parameter, so the Iterate cannot be sent to a task, and the checker says which
;; field: `closure capture s, field f of Iterate`. The pure struct therefore does not by itself give what D7 weighs it
;; for (a seq that crosses a task, unlike an LSeq): that takes a colour parameter, (defstruct (Iterate a k :colour) ..),
;; which changes the type of the page's row to (Iterate a k) and the three lines of IterateCur in fib.seq.cursors. Y1 ran
;; that variant in a scratch copy of the library and this program was then accepted. If the owner chooses it, this
;; case flips to `accept` and 2228 gains an iterate.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq))

(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((s (iterate (fn (x: i64) (+ x 1)) 0)))
    (let ((h (spawn (fn () (reduce (fn (a x) (+ a x)) 0 (take 5 s))))))
      (join h))))
